<newsitem itemid="208063" id="root" date="1996-11-21" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Storehouse profits rise 13 pct in first half.</title>
<headline>Storehouse profits rise 13 pct in first half.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>28 weeks to October 12</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)preexceps   6.1		    vs 5.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.3		    vs 3.0</p>
<p> Pretax preexceps	 37.5		   vs 33.3</p>
<p> Turnover		   590.5		  vs 518.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pretax profits were in a range of 35.5 to 37.5 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 37.1		   vs 30.0</p>
<p> Exceptional charge     20.5		   vs 1.2 gain</p>
<p> Interest received	0.4		    vs 3.3</p>
<p> Tax			  8.9		    vs 11.0</p>
<p> Net taxed		  8.1		    vs 23.5</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 11 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  December 24</p>
<p> Ex-div date		December 16</p>
<p>NOTE - The exceptional charge relates to the restructuring of Childrens World, which Storehouse bought from Boots Co Plc, and the sale of Blazer to Moss Bros Plc. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
